Z||000000||CUTTER||10-03-1999||01:53 AM||||I have a 87GT and every time I start up my car the temp needle goes all the way to the other side and back to 0 again. and stays there and moves the slightest bit when driving(so little you can barely see it)Is this a prob or was some kind of mod been done to it, or just going on the fritz? what could the problem be?<BR> Thanks, Shane||||reg||5
Z||000001||K9||10-03-1999||07:05 AM||||Hay Cutter, I have the exact same problem in my 85GT.I have changed the temp sender unit,checked every wire and connection but still havent been able to fix the problem.I have just got a new temp/fuel gage. I will be replaceing the old one with in the next week. I will let you Know if this fixes my problem.||||reg||11
Z||000002||batboy||10-03-1999||08:58 AM||||Fiero temp gauge needles normally "pegs" when you first crank the engine then settles back down when the engine starts. After the engine warms up though, it should work normally.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phil||10-03-1999||09:18 AM||||One way of stopping the pegging is to reverse the green wires at the sender and at the instrument panel(temp gage and idiot light)||||reg||1
